# Cursor AI Rules for iAm Monorepo

## Quick Start
- Read CLAUDE.md first for complete context and patterns
- This monorepo follows strict patterns - match them exactly
- All standards are documented in docs/standards/

## Key Principles
1. Spec-driven: Read SPEC.md before implementing
2. Vertical slices: Code organized by domain, not layer
3. Type safety: Annotate all functions, no 'any'
4. Consistency: Match existing patterns exactly
5. Test everything: Unit + integration tests required

## File Naming
- Services: `userAuthentication.service.ts`
- Entities: `user.entity.ts`
- Validators: `loginInput.validator.ts`
- Procedures: `login.procedure.ts`
- Tests: `userAuthentication.service.unit.test.ts`

## Standards
- Read: docs/standards/ROOT-STANDARDS.md
- For domains: docs/standards/packages/DOMAIN-STANDARDS.md
- TypeScript: strict mode, always annotate returns
- Imports: external → internal → relative
- Errors: Create domain-specific error classes

## Dependencies
- Domain can use: Platform, Shared
- Platform can use: Shared
- Shared can use: Shared
- Domain → Domain requires approval

## Before Implementing
1. Check relevant SPEC.md
2. Review DOMAIN-STANDARDS.md for pattern
3. Look at one existing example
4. Match the pattern exactly
5. Write tests alongside code

## Available Packages
- @iam/shared-types, @iam/shared-utils, @iam/shared-constants, @iam/shared-config
- @iam/database (Prisma), @iam/cache (Redis), @iam/jobs (BullMQ)

## Common Commands
- pnpm test - Run tests
- pnpm typecheck - Type check all
- pnpm lint - Lint all
- pnpm format - Format all
- pnpm --filter @iam/[package] [command] - Run for specific package

## Remember
This codebase is designed FOR AI. Trust the structure, follow the patterns, ship quality code.

Full context: CLAUDE.md
